<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">European Union</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The European Union is a political and economic union of European states, developed from the European communities founded in the 1950s. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a>, which united much of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, are often invoked as symbolic forerunners of European unity in discussions of the EU.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/european-union.jpg" alt="European Union" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Verdy p, User:-xfi-, User:Paddu, User:Nightstallion, User:Funakoshi, User:Jeltz, User:Dbenbenn, User:Zscout370 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Europe.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
